Dear Quality Management Team,

Your CE certification for the Gateway Product Family (Certificate No.
DE-CA-2024-8842) will expire on 15 November 2026. Without a valid CE
mark, your products cannot be sold in the EEA.

Certificate Details:
  Certificate Number: DE-CA-2024-8842
  Certificate Type: CE Marking — LVD 2014/35/EU
  Product Family: Email Security Gateway (GW-1000/2000/5000)
  Standards: EN 62368-1:2020
  Notified Body: TÜV Rheinland LGA Products GmbH (NB 0197)
  Expiry: 2026-11-15 (22 days remaining)

Consequences of Expiry:
  - Immediate sales ban in 30 EEA countries
  - Customs seizure at EU borders
  - Recall obligation for products in market
  - Fines up to €500,000 per violation
  - Distributor liability
  - Loss of EU customer contracts

Renewal Process:

  Step 1 — Submit Technical Documentation:
  Navigate to our Certipedia portal manually:
  www.certipedia.com (type URL manually)
  → Client Login → Certificate DE-CA-2024-8842
  → Upload Documents

  Required documents:
  1. Updated Risk Assessment (EN 62368-1 Annex B)
  2. Technical Construction File (TCF)
  3. Schematics & PCB layouts
  4. Bill of Materials (BOM) with safety-critical items
  5. Test Reports (EMC & Safety, from accredited lab)
  6. User Manual (EU languages)
  7. Declaration of Conformity (draft)
  8. Factory Production Control documentation

  Important Security Notes:
  TÜV Rheinland will NEVER:
  - Send you a direct "Upload" link via email
  - Use Microsoft Azure AD B2B for portal authentication
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth token
  - Cite "large file upload session maintenance" as reason for tokens

  All document submissions happen at certipedia.com when you
  navigate there manually. If you receive an email with an
  "Upload" button or Azure AD authentication, it is a phishing
  attempt targeting CE certification holders.

  Client portal credentials are sent by post to the registered
  manufacturer address (not via email).

Step 2 — Factory Inspection:
  Duration: 1-2 days at Hangzhou facility
  Cost: €2,800 (included in renewal)

Step 3 — Renewal Fee:
  Certification renewal (3 models): €6,500
  Factory inspection: €2,800
  Document review: €1,200
  Total: €10,500

Timeline:
  10/24  Submit documentation
  10/25-11/01  Document review
  11/04-06  Factory inspection
  11/08  Review results
  11/12  Certificate issuance
  11/15  Current certificate expires

